---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Loading from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Loading.astro";
---
<Docs title="Motion" lede="Interface parts arrive with an ease-out. Things that fall, fall with gravity. Nothing moves just to be seen.">
  <h2>Two curves</h2>
  <div class="mo">
    <div class="mo__track"><span class="mo__ball mo__ball--out"></span></div>
    <p><code>--ply-ease-out</code>, <code>cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)</code>. Fast start, long settle. For menus, cards, tooltips, anything arriving.</p>
    <div class="mo__track mo__track--v"><span class="mo__ball mo__ball--gravity"></span></div>
    <p><code>--ply-ease-gravity</code>, <code>cubic-bezier(0.55, 0, 1, 0.45)</code>. Slow start, speeding up. For balls dropping through the machine and anything else that falls.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Durations</h2>
  <div class="ply-table-wrap">
    <table class="ply-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Value</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>--ply-duration-fast</code></td><td>120ms</td><td>Hover and press feedback, color changes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--ply-duration-base</code></td><td>200ms</td><td>Switches, tooltips, small reveals.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--ply-duration-slow</code></td><td>320ms</td><td>Toasts and panels entering.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--ply-duration-drop</code></td><td>900ms</td><td>One ball falling the height of the machine.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>The signature moment</h2>
  <p>Each page gets at most one moment of motion, and it shows a process. On these docs it is the probability machine filling on load. The same machine, small, is the loading indicator: <Loading label="Loading example" /></p>

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>When the reader asks their system for reduced motion, every animation jumps to its end state. The machine draws its settled bell curve, the loading indicator shows a resting ball, and transitions take effect at once. The CSS reset handles this globally; scripts check <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> before animating.</p>
</Docs>
<style>
  .mo { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr; gap: var(--ply-space-5); align-items: center; }
  .mo__track { position: relative; height: 2.5rem; border-bottom: 3px solid var(--ply-color-rule-strong); }
  .mo__track--v { height: 6rem; width: 2.5rem; border-bottom: 3px solid var(--ply-color-rule-strong); justify-self: center; }
  .mo__ball { position: absolute; width: 1rem; height: 1rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--ply-color-accent); bottom: 0; }
  .mo__ball--out { left: 0; animation: mo-out 2.4s var(--ply-ease-out) infinite; }
  .mo__ball--gravity { left: 50%; margin-left: -0.5rem; animation: mo-fall 1.6s var(--ply-ease-gravity) infinite; }
  @keyframes mo-out { 0%, 15% { transform: translateX(0); } 60%, 100% { transform: translateX(7.5rem); } }
  @keyframes mo-fall { 0% { transform: translateY(-5rem); opacity: 0; } 10% { opacity: 1; } 70%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .mo__ball--out { transform: translateX(7.5rem); } }
</style>
